Luminescence by Martijn Steinrucken (BigWings), 2017
https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/blob/master/procedural/bigwings-luminescence.glsl
(raw file: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/master/procedural/bigwings-luminescence.glsl)

The author's notice in the shader's own header (line 108 of the file above)
reads, verbatim:

    License Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License.

Credit: the shader and its look are the work of Martijn Steinrucken (BigWings).
The shader's header also credits Klaus Lunde for the music that accompanied the
original entry; no music is used here. Inside the code, three small helper
functions are credited by the author to other people: a hash function (Dave
Hoskins), smooth min / max (Inigo Quilez) and pModPolar (hg_sdf, mercury.sexy).
The author's header applies the licence above to the file as a whole.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper. This port is an
adaptation of the original shader and is offered under the same licence,
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported. It may not
be used commercially.

What was changed (the note at the top of main.metal lists it too):
  - the libretro wrapper (vertex stage, uniforms, one unused parameter and
    main()) was removed;
  - the clock runs at half speed (LW_TIME_SCALE = 0.5) so the scene is calmer
    as a desktop background;
  - the camera follows the author's own automatic path; there is no mouse input;
  - GLSL constructs were rewritten for Metal (a struct member renamed, an inout
    parameter passed by value, step() and mat3 written out, smoothstep written
    out as its formula because it is called with reversed edges);
  - uninitialised values were initialised, and two clamps (acos argument, final
    colour before pow) were added so no NaN can appear in tall or wide views;
  - unused code (the SINGLE and MOUSE branches and five unused helper
    functions) was dropped.
The marching, the shapes, the constants and the shading are the author's.

